1
00:00:00,450 --> 00:00:01,958
Look at a town map.

2
00:00:01,958 --> 00:00:06,460
Some roads run side by side, and
never meet, however far they go.

3
00:00:06,860 --> 00:00:11,626
Other roads cross each other perfectly
square, like the corner of a page.

4
00:00:12,076 --> 00:00:15,047
Diya spots both kinds on
the map of her college town.

5
00:00:15,397 --> 00:00:17,918
How can you tell, without
drawing them forever?

6
00:00:18,418 --> 00:00:20,707
The secret is hiding in their slopes.

7
00:00:20,707 --> 00:00:21,833
Let us find it.

8
00:00:22,483 --> 00:00:24,226
Start with parallel lines.

9
00:00:24,226 --> 00:00:28,373
Parallel means they stay the same
distance apart, and never meet.

10
00:00:28,773 --> 00:00:31,083
Here are two lines on graph paper.

11
00:00:31,083 --> 00:00:34,652
Each one climbs one step up
for every two steps across.

12
00:00:35,052 --> 00:00:37,222
Same rise, same run, same slope.

13
00:00:37,222 --> 00:00:40,933
They lean by the same amount,
so one never catches the other.

14
00:00:41,533 --> 00:00:45,866
The rule: two non vertical lines are
parallel exactly when their slopes

15
00:00:45,866 --> 00:00:46,766
are equal.

16
00:00:46,719 --> 00:00:48,189
m one equals m two.

17
00:00:48,839 --> 00:00:52,498
Now let us turn one line, and
watch where the two lines meet.

18
00:00:52,898 --> 00:00:54,828
Line one has slope one half.

19
00:00:54,828 --> 00:00:57,489
Line two starts steep, and slowly turns.

20
00:00:57,889 --> 00:01:02,123
As the two slopes get closer, the
meeting point runs further and further

21
00:01:02,123 --> 00:01:03,023
away.

22
00:01:03,047 --> 00:01:06,735
When the slopes are equal, there
is no meeting point at all.

23
00:01:06,735 --> 00:01:08,221
The lines are parallel.

24
00:01:08,821 --> 00:01:09,721
Keep turning.

25
00:01:09,639 --> 00:01:12,601
Watch the crossing angle, and
the two slopes multiplied.

26
00:01:13,001 --> 00:01:16,899
At exactly ninety degrees, the
slopes are one half and minus two.

27
00:01:16,899 --> 00:01:18,614
Their product is minus one.

28
00:01:19,264 --> 00:01:20,348
Why minus one?

29
00:01:20,348 --> 00:01:23,408
Take line one, with a
right triangle under it.

30
00:01:23,408 --> 00:01:24,837
Run two, rise one.

31
00:01:24,837 --> 00:01:25,969
Slope one half.

32
00:01:26,369 --> 00:01:27,269
Step one.

33
00:01:27,203 --> 00:01:30,379
Turn the picture a quarter
turn, anticlockwise.

34
00:01:31,129 --> 00:01:32,029
Step two.

35
00:01:31,815 --> 00:01:33,590
The run of two now points up.

36
00:01:33,590 --> 00:01:35,148
It becomes a rise of two.

37
00:01:35,898 --> 00:01:36,798
Step three.

38
00:01:36,717 --> 00:01:38,738
The rise of one now points left.

39
00:01:38,738 --> 00:01:40,670
It becomes a run of minus one.

40
00:01:41,420 --> 00:01:42,320
Step four.

41
00:01:42,293 --> 00:01:46,178
The new slope is two over
minus one, which is minus two.

42
00:01:46,178 --> 00:01:49,079
And one half times minus two is minus one.

43
00:01:49,829 --> 00:01:54,286
So two non vertical lines are
perpendicular exactly when m one times m

44
00:01:54,286 --> 00:01:55,665
two is minus one.

45
00:01:55,665 --> 00:01:58,310
Flip the slope, and change its sign.

46
00:01:58,960 --> 00:02:00,030
Side by side.

47
00:02:00,030 --> 00:02:02,369
Parallel lines have the same slope.

48
00:02:02,369 --> 00:02:03,538
Two, and two.

49
00:02:03,938 --> 00:02:07,521
Perpendicular lines: flip the
slope and change its sign.

50
00:02:07,521 --> 00:02:09,317
Two, and minus one half.

51
00:02:09,917 --> 00:02:10,817
Your turn.

52
00:02:10,750 --> 00:02:12,473
One line has slope three.

53
00:02:12,473 --> 00:02:14,684
Another has slope minus one third.

54
00:02:14,684 --> 00:02:17,067
Parallel, perpendicular, or neither?

55
00:02:17,067 --> 00:02:18,292
Pause and decide.

56
00:02:21,492 --> 00:02:22,495
Perpendicular!

57
00:02:22,495 --> 00:02:25,256
Three times minus one third is minus one.

58
00:02:25,906 --> 00:02:27,017
Remember this.

59
00:02:27,017 --> 00:02:29,301
Parallel lines have equal slopes.

60
00:02:29,301 --> 00:02:32,167
Perpendicular slopes
multiply to minus one.

61
00:02:32,867 --> 00:02:34,572
Most lines are neither.

62
00:02:34,572 --> 00:02:36,818
They cross at some other angle.

63
00:02:36,818 --> 00:02:37,718
How big?

64
00:02:38,018 --> 00:02:42,625
Each line makes its own angle with
the x axis, alpha one and alpha two.

65
00:02:42,625 --> 00:02:45,793
Their slopes are tan alpha
one and tan alpha two.

66
00:02:46,193 --> 00:02:47,093
Step one.

67
00:02:47,008 --> 00:02:51,764
The angle between the lines is the
difference, alpha two minus alpha one.

68
00:02:52,514 --> 00:02:53,414
Step two.

69
00:02:53,297 --> 00:02:56,439
Use the tan of a difference,
from chapter three.

70
00:02:57,189 --> 00:02:58,131
Step three.

71
00:02:58,131 --> 00:02:59,554
Put in the slopes.

72
00:02:59,554 --> 00:03:04,172
tan theta is m two minus m one,
over one plus m one times m two.

73
00:03:04,922 --> 00:03:05,822
Step four.

74
00:03:05,686 --> 00:03:07,627
Take the size, with a modulus.

75
00:03:07,627 --> 00:03:10,737
That gives the sharp angle,
less than ninety degrees.

76
00:03:11,387 --> 00:03:12,480
Side by side.

77
00:03:12,480 --> 00:03:17,425
Where two lines cross, they make a
sharp angle, theta, and a wide angle,

78
00:03:17,425 --> 00:03:19,084
one eighty minus theta.

79
00:03:19,684 --> 00:03:20,584
Quick one.

80
00:03:20,543 --> 00:03:24,542
Can this formula find the angle
between two perpendicular lines?

81
00:03:24,542 --> 00:03:25,756
Pause and think.

82
00:03:28,956 --> 00:03:29,856
No!

83
00:03:29,418 --> 00:03:34,344
For perpendicular lines, one plus m
one m two is zero, and we cannot divide

84
00:03:34,344 --> 00:03:35,244
by zero.

85
00:03:35,118 --> 00:03:37,390
But that angle is ninety degrees.

86
00:03:38,040 --> 00:03:39,730
Now, one worked example.

87
00:03:40,080 --> 00:03:44,469
Find the sharp angle between two
lines with slopes two and minus three.

88
00:03:44,969 --> 00:03:45,869
Step one.

89
00:03:45,813 --> 00:03:46,713
Top.

90
00:03:46,339 --> 00:03:49,429
m two minus m one is
minus three minus two.

91
00:03:49,429 --> 00:03:50,913
That is minus five.

92
00:03:51,663 --> 00:03:52,563
Step two.

93
00:03:52,543 --> 00:03:53,443
Bottom.

94
00:03:53,251 --> 00:03:56,920
One plus m one times m
two is one plus minus six.

95
00:03:56,920 --> 00:03:58,465
That is minus five.

96
00:03:59,215 --> 00:04:00,177
Step three.

97
00:04:00,177 --> 00:04:04,871
tan theta is the size of minus
five over minus five, which is one.

98
00:04:05,621 --> 00:04:06,521
Step four.

99
00:04:06,442 --> 00:04:09,839
tan theta equals one, so
theta is forty five degrees.

100
00:04:10,489 --> 00:04:11,951
Now, the exam trap.

101
00:04:12,301 --> 00:04:13,790
A line has slope two.

102
00:04:13,790 --> 00:04:15,699
Slope of a perpendicular line?

103
00:04:15,699 --> 00:04:19,190
Many students just change the
sign, and write minus two.

104
00:04:19,590 --> 00:04:23,352
But two times minus two is
minus four, not minus one.

105
00:04:23,352 --> 00:04:24,678
Flip it as well.

106
00:04:24,678 --> 00:04:26,796
The answer is minus one half.

107
00:04:27,445 --> 00:04:28,878
Where is this asked?

108
00:04:28,878 --> 00:04:33,619
In JEE Main, for example in January
twenty nineteen: find a missing coordinate

109
00:04:33,619 --> 00:04:35,937
so that two lines are perpendicular.

110
00:04:36,537 --> 00:04:37,665
Exam level now.

111
00:04:37,665 --> 00:04:40,764
L one passes through the
origin and one, three.

112
00:04:40,764 --> 00:04:45,153
L two has positive slope m, and
makes forty five degrees with L one.

113
00:04:45,153 --> 00:04:46,053
Find m.

114
00:04:45,841 --> 00:04:47,017
Pause and solve.

115
00:04:52,417 --> 00:04:53,876
The answer is C.

116
00:04:53,876 --> 00:04:54,804
One half.

117
00:04:55,304 --> 00:04:58,787
L one has slope three,
and tan forty five is one.

118
00:04:59,287 --> 00:05:04,315
Without the modulus, m minus three
is plus or minus, one plus three m.

119
00:05:04,815 --> 00:05:07,143
Plus gives m equals minus two.

120
00:05:07,143 --> 00:05:09,350
Not positive, so reject it.

121
00:05:09,350 --> 00:05:13,113
Minus gives four m equals
two, so m is one half.

122
00:05:13,713 --> 00:05:15,253
Here is your recap.

123
00:05:15,253 --> 00:05:16,836
Screenshot this card.

124
00:05:20,036 --> 00:05:22,222
Can you answer these three
questions without help?

125
00:05:22,622 --> 00:05:23,522
One.

126
00:05:23,066 --> 00:05:26,983
What is the slope of a line parallel
to a line of slope minus four?

127
00:05:27,883 --> 00:05:28,783
Two.

128
00:05:28,328 --> 00:05:31,791
Lines with slopes one half and
minus two meet at what angle?

129
00:05:32,691 --> 00:05:33,591
Three.

130
00:05:33,286 --> 00:05:36,787
Why does the angle formula
fail for perpendicular lines?

131
00:05:37,887 --> 00:05:40,026
Next time: two dots on a map.

132
00:05:40,026 --> 00:05:43,148
Draw the road between
them, and write its rule.

133
00:05:43,148 --> 00:05:45,278
Point slope and two point forms.
